body:
Adding a transformData to the widget breaks the noResultsTemplate. If I have no data it does not pull up the empty template. 

`search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.hits({
      container: '#hits',
      hitsPerPage: 10,
      templates: {
 item: newTemplate2Panel,
          empty: noResultsTemplate
      },
      transformData: function (hit) {
          hit.skills = [];
          try
          {
              for (var i = 0; i < hit.Skills.length; i++) {
                  hit.skills.push(hit.Skills[i].SkillName)
              }
              hit.RunDate = jQuery.timeago(hit.RunDate);
  return hit;
          }
          catch(err) { 
          } }}));`

comments.body:
Yes, you need to use this:

``` js
instantsearch.widgets.hits({
  transformData: {
    item: function() {},
    empty: function() {}
  }
});
```

Let me know if this fixes the issue
